ll/story/_/id/50510750/cfp-top-25-postseason-x-factor","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"QB rankings for all 68 Power 4 college football teams","description":"We're nearing the end of the season. How have our opinions about the top quarterbacks changed?","published":"2026-11-18T11:43:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50510847/ranking-power-4-qbs","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL mock draft: Reid's midseason first-round predictions for all 32 picks","description":"Which NFL team could land Drew Mestemaker? Who needs Chris Cole, Ashton Hampton or Jamari Johnson? Jordan Reid projected first-round picks for 2027 -- and a trade.","published":"2026-11-18T15:09:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50502243/2027-nfl-mock-draft-reid-midseason-32-first-round-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"Jordan Reid","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft: Dolphins, Titans, Eagles, Jets, Chargers in race for No. 1 pick","description":"Five NFL teams have at least 5% odds to land the No. 1 pick in 2027, per ESPN's Football Power Index: the Dolphins, Titans, Eagles, Jets and Chargers.","published":"2026-11-18T13:32:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50510863/2027-nfl-draft-top-pick-dolphins-titans-eagles-jets-chargers","type":"Story","byline":"NFL Nation, Jordan Reid and Seth Walder","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Anger Index: Why Texas Tech, Tennessee and the Group of 6 should be mad","description":"Ranking the teams who should be most upset about their latest CFP ranking.","published":"2026-11-18T04:25:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50510905/cfp-ranking-2026-anger-index-texas-tech","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922989/jelani-mcdonald","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jelani_McDonald"},"pick":{"pick":40,"round":2,"team":"IND","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jelani McDonald","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jelani_McDonald","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-17T20:11:56Z","intro":"Jelani McDonald is an American college football safety for the Texas Longhorns.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"McDonald attended Connally High School in Waco, Texas, where he played both defensive back and quarterback. As a senior, he was the Offensive MVP of District 11-4A Division 2 after rushing 77 times for 852 yards with nine touchdowns, and passing for 707 yards with 13 touchdowns. On defense he had 25 tackles, four sacks and an interception. McDonald was selected to play in the 2023 All-American Bowl. He committed to play college football at the University of Texas at Austin."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at Texas in 2023, McDonald played in 12 games and had two tackles. As a sophomore in 2024, he played in 14 games with four starts and recorded 33 tackles and one interception.\nMcDonald became a starting safety his junior year in 2025. In the first four weeks of the 2025 season, McDonald contributed to three turnovers in three consecutive games, logging one fumble recovery for 24 yards against San Jose State, one interception for 16 yards against UTEP, and one interception against Sam Houston. He ended the season with 80 tackles, three interceptions, and one fumble recovery.\nFor the 2026 season, McDonald chose to return for his senior year and continued as the starting safety. In Week 11 against LSU, McDonald recorded three interceptions, becoming the first SEC player to record three interceptions in a single game since 2020. For his performance, McDonald was named Player of the Week by the Associated Press, Chuck Bednarik Award,  Jim Thorpe Award, and Walter Camp Award."}]}}